UNIT isNumber
KIND FUNCTIONAL
ORACLE-CLASS deterministic
SIG isNumber(value: any) -> boolean
DEPENDS-ON none

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OVERVIEW
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# isNumber is a pure, total, side-effect-free type predicate. It returns true
# iff `value` is "classified as a Number" in the lodash-3.x sense: it is either
# a primitive number, OR it is an object-like value whose internal [[Class]]
# brand (as exposed by Object.prototype.toString) is exactly "[object Number]"
# (i.e. a boxed Number object such as `new Number(0)`). For ALL other inputs it
# returns false. It NEVER throws and NEVER mutates the argument or any state.
# There is no ambient seam (no clock / RNG / env / io / net) — fully
# deterministic.
#
# IMPORTANT classification notes (these are the contract, not incidental):
#   - NaN, Infinity, -Infinity are ALL numbers  -> true. (To EXCLUDE these the
#     real library directs callers to isFinite; isNumber itself does NOT exclude
#     them.)
#   - A boxed Number object (`new Number(x)`) is true regardless of its wrapped
#     value (including new Number(0), whose +valueOf is 0/falsy).
#   - A numeric STRING ('5') is NOT a number -> false. No coercion/parsing is
#     performed; the predicate inspects type/brand only, never the textual or
#     numeric content of the value.
#   - bigint (e.g. 5n) is NOT a number under this predicate -> false. (typeof
#     5n === 'bigint', not 'number'; and its brand is not '[object Number]'.)
#       The original was authored pre-bigint, but its logic gives false here,
#       which is the observed and contractually-required behavior.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BEHAVIOR  (exact pipeline — ordered, short-circuit OR)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Two helper notions, then the predicate. Reproduce EXACTLY.
#
# HELPER isObjectLike(value):
#   return  (value is truthy)  AND  (typeof value == 'object')
#   # i.e. in JS:  !!value && typeof value == 'object'
#   # Consequences of this exact form:
#   #   - null            -> !!null is false                       -> false
#   #   - undefined       -> !!undefined is false                  -> false
#   #   - 0 / NaN / '' / false (falsy primitives) -> !!value false -> false
#   #   - {} , [] , new Number(0), new Date(), /x/, function value -> typeof is
#   #         'object' (or 'function' for functions) ...
#   #         NB: typeof function == 'function' (NOT 'object'), so a function is
#   #         NOT object-like here -> isObjectLike(fn) is false.
#   #   - any non-null value with typeof 'object' (plain object, array, boxed
#   #         Number/String/Boolean, Date, RegExp, Map, Set, typed array,
#   #         Buffer, etc.) -> true.
#
# CONSTANT numberTag = "[object Number]"        # exact string, byte-for-byte
# CONSTANT objectToString = Object.prototype.toString   # the ORIGINAL, unpatched
#                                                        # Object#toString
#
# PREDICATE isNumber(value):
#   #  NODE 1 (primitive fast-path, short-circuits the OR):
#   if  typeof value == 'number'  -> return true
#   #     (covers every number primitive: integers, floats, ±0, NaN,
#   #      Infinity, -Infinity, Number.MIN_VALUE, Number.MAX_VALUE, etc.)
#   #
#   #  NODE 2 (boxed-Number branch — only reached when NODE 1 is false):
#   if  isObjectLike(value)  AND  objectToString.call(value) == numberTag
#         -> return true
#   #     objectToString.call(value) yields the [[Class]]/brand string, e.g.
#   #     "[object Number]" for new Number(0), "[object Object]" for {},
#   #     "[object Array]" for [], "[object Date]" for a Date,
#   #     "[object RegExp]" for /x/, "[object String]" for new String(''),
#   #     "[object Boolean]" for new Boolean(false), "[object Map]", etc.
#   #     ONLY "[object Number]" passes this branch.
#   #
#   #  NODE 3 (default):
#   return false
#
# OBSERVABLE TRUTH TABLE (decision = NODE that fires; verified against the real
# package lodash.isnumber@3.0.3). The blind re-emitter MUST reproduce all rows:
#
#   value                              typeof        brand               -> result
#   ---------------------------------  ------------  ------------------  --------
#   0, 1, -1, 3.14, -2.5              'number'      (n/a, NODE1)        -> true
#   ±0, 1e308, 5e-324 (MIN_VALUE)     'number'      (NODE1)            -> true
#   NaN                               'number'      (NODE1)            -> true
#   Infinity                          'number'      (NODE1)            -> true
#   -Infinity                         'number'      (NODE1)            -> true
#   new Number(0)                     'object'      [object Number]    -> true
#   new Number(5)                     'object'      [object Number]    -> true
#   '5'  (numeric string)             'string'      ----               -> false
#   ''   (empty string)               'string'      ----               -> false
#   'NaN' / 'Infinity' (strings)      'string'      ----               -> false
#   null                              'object'*     (isObjectLike F)   -> false
#       (*typeof null=='object' but !!null is false -> not object-like)
#   undefined                         'undefined'   ----               -> false
#   true                              'boolean'     ----               -> false
#   false                             'boolean'     ----               -> false
#   {} (plain object)                 'object'      [object Object]    -> false
#   {a:1}                             'object'      [object Object]    -> false
#   [] (array)                        'object'      [object Array]     -> false
#   [1,2,3]                           'object'      [object Array]     -> false
#   5n  (bigint)                      'bigint'      ----               -> false
#   0n  (bigint)                      'bigint'      ----               -> false
#   /x/  (RegExp)                     'object'      [object RegExp]    -> false
#   new Date(0)                       'object'      [object Date]      -> false
#   new String('5')                   'object'      [object String]    -> false
#   new Boolean(true)                 'object'      [object Boolean]   -> false
#   new Map()                         'object'      [object Map]       -> false
#   new Set()                         'object'      [object Set]       -> false
#   new Uint8Array(n)                 'object'      [object Uint8Array]-> false
#   Buffer.from([..])                 'object'      [object Uint8Array]-> false
#
# NOTE on Buffer: Node Buffers are Uint8Array subclasses; their brand is
# "[object Uint8Array]" (not "[object Number]") -> false. Confirmed live.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ERROR / THROW BEHAVIOR
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# None. The function performs only typeof checks and a single
# Object.prototype.toString.call — neither throws for any value. There is no
# input that causes isNumber to throw. (It also does not read any property of
# the value other than via toString's internal brand lookup, so no getter on
# the value is invoked except the engine-internal [[Class]] resolution, which
# is not user-observable here.) total function.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ORACLE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ORACLE value -> oracle.json
# Pure value-mode: for each generated [value], the expected is the boolean
# isNumber(value). No seam, no trace. Deterministic.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SCOPE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IN-CONTRACT LOGIC (reproduce exactly): the entire predicate above — the
#   typeof=='number' fast path, the isObjectLike && brand=='[object Number]'
#   branch, the exact numberTag string, and the false default. This is the
#   whole unit; there is no carried data.
#
# CARRIED DATA: none. (No tables; the only literal is the 16-char tag string
#   "[object Number]", which is reproduced inline in the SIR above, not a
#   carried table.)
#
# OUT-OF-CONTRACT / OUT-OF-ENVELOPE (documented, NOT emitted by genInputs
#   because the oracle codec cannot round-trip them; a blind re-emitter still
#   reconstructs the behavior from the rows below):
#     - Symbol values (typeof 'symbol'): NODE1 false, NODE2 false -> result
#       false. Not emitted (symbols do not survive JSON encode).
#     - Live function values (typeof 'function'): isObjectLike is false because
#       typeof != 'object' -> result false. Not emitted (functions do not
#       round-trip and bear identity).
#     - A boxed value with a TAMPERED/spoofed Symbol.toStringTag making
#       Object.prototype.toString.call(value) return "[object Number]" would
#       pass NODE2 -> true. This is an adversarial, non-codec-faithful,
#       identity-bearing object and is out of envelope; not emitted. (Documented
#       so the contract is complete: the predicate trusts the unpatched
#       Object#toString brand.)

